# Agent sessions

Start by reading `README.md` and listing `src/`.
Do not scan `node_modules`, `dist`, or coverage.

Restate the user goal in one sentence, then touch only files required.

Prefer editing existing stubs over new abstractions.

Run `pnpm typecheck` and `pnpm test` after code changes.
Do not start long watch processes.

If blocked on product decisions (advisory source, semver policy, monorepo support), ask — do not guess.

Keep answers short.
Put detail in code and README, not in new markdown files.

Do not add README sections, badges, or architecture diagrams unless asked.
